From 9c4e96f7627123d1d32bca2769b8a396114d83f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 16:43:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: do not log a deferred CSIPHY lookup as an
 error

When the CSI PHYs are separate devices, msm_csiphy_subdev_init() gets
them with devm_phy_get_by_of_node(), which returns -EPROBE_DEFER until
the PHY driver has bound. camss_init_subdevices() reports every failure
with dev_err(), so a CAMSS module that loads before the PHY module, as
it can when udev loads both at boot, prints "csiphy 4 init fail" and
then binds normally on the retry.

Use dev_err_probe(): real errors are still printed, a deferral is
recorded as the deferred-probe reason instead.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c | 8 +++-----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
index 80d47b3028..22d8c95c34 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -5215,11 +5215,9 @@ static int camss_init_subdevices(struct camss *camss)
 							    res->csiphy_res[i].csiphy.id);
 		}
 
-		if (ret < 0) {
-			dev_err(camss->dev, "csiphy %d init fail\n",
-				res->csiphy_res[i].csiphy.id);
-			return ret;
-		}
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return dev_err_probe(camss->dev, ret, "csiphy %d init fail\n",
+					     res->csiphy_res[i].csiphy.id);
 	}
 
 	if (camss->tpg) {
